{
 "title": "Why a² + b² = c² works",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "A right triangle",
   "say": "Take a right triangle with legs a and b and hypotenuse c. The hypotenuse is the side opposite the right angle.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "title",
     "x": 60,
     "y": 40,
     "text": "Why a² + b² = c² works",
     "size": 54
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "tri",
     "d": "M300,560 L540,560 L300,380 Z",
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lab-a",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 525,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lab-b",
     "x": 255,
     "y": 455,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lab-c",
     "x": 360,
     "y": 480,
     "text": "c",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "red"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Squares on the sides",
   "say": "Build a square on each side. Its area is the side length squared, so the squares have areas a², b² and c².",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "sq-a",
     "x": 300,
     "y": 560,
     "w": 240,
     "h": 240,
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 3,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "sq-b",
     "x": 60,
     "y": 380,
     "w": 240,
     "h": 180,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 3,
     "fill": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "sq-c",
     "d": "M300,380 L540,560 L720,320 L480,140 Z",
     "color": "red",
     "width": 3,
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "area-a",
     "x": 420,
     "y": 660,
     "text": "a²",
     "size": 44,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "area-b",
     "x": 180,
     "y": 450,
     "text": "b²",
     "size": 44,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "area-c",
     "x": 510,
     "y": 330,
     "text": "c²",
     "size": 44,
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "A big square",
   "say": "Now draw a square with side a + b. Its area is (a + b)², which we can also count in another way.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "big",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 200,
     "w": 420,
     "h": 420,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "big-label",
     "x": 1010,
     "y": 150,
     "text": "side a + b",
     "size": 34,
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Four copies of the triangle",
   "say": "Put four copies of the triangle into the corners of the big square. Each copy has legs a and b.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "t1",
     "d": "M800,200 L1040,200 L800,380 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "t2",
     "d": "M1040,200 L1220,200 L1220,440 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "t3",
     "d": "M1220,440 L1220,620 L980,620 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "t4",
     "d": "M800,620 L980,620 L800,380 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "The square left in the middle",
   "say": "The four triangles leave a tilted square in the middle. Its side is the hypotenuse c, so its area is c².",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "inner",
     "d": "M1040,200 L1220,440 L980,620 L800,380 Z",
     "color": "red",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "inner-label",
     "x": 1010,
     "y": 385,
     "text": "c²",
     "size": 44,
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Count the area two ways",
   "say": "The big square's area is (a + b)² and also four triangles plus c². Both count the same area, so the a and b terms must match up and leave c² = a² + b².",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "erase",
     "region": {
      "x": 40,
      "y": 100,
      "w": 560,
      "h": 760
     }
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq1",
     "x": 60,
     "y": 300,
     "text": "Big square: (a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b²",
     "size": 36
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq2",
     "x": 60,
     "y": 380,
     "text": "Four triangles + c²: 4·(ab/2) + c² = 2ab + c²",
     "size": 36
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq3",
     "x": 60,
     "y": 480,
     "text": "Both equal the same area, so",
     "size": 36
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq4",
     "x": 60,
     "y": 540,
     "text": "a² + b² = c²",
     "size": 56,
     "color": "blue",
     "underline": true
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}